   "id": "nasa",
   "url": "https://www.nasa.gov/missions/artemis/space-suit-cost/",
   "domain": "nasa.gov",
   "title": "A full NASA space suit costs $12 million",
   "excerpt": "Why the suits astronauts wear outside the station cost as much as a small spacecraft — and where the money goes.",
   "articleText": [
    "The suit astronauts wear outside the station is less a garment than a small spacecraft. It carries its own oxygen, cooling, power and radio, and every one of those systems has to keep working for hours in vacuum.",
    "Most of the cost isn’t in the materials. It’s in the testing: each layer is qualified on its own, then again as part of the whole suit.",
    "Only a handful of the current suits are flight-ready at any time, which is why each one is maintained, refitted and reused for decades rather than replaced.",
    "The next generation is being built to fit a wider range of body sizes — a change that sounds small and touches almost every part of the design."
   ],
